2026-11-13T05:37:58.7192727Z # LexMachina Factory Architecture
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7192949Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7193108Z ## Current product architecture
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7193341Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7193565Z LexMachina is a **query-specific visual legal-research system**.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7193886Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7193997Z Canonical data flow:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7194155Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7194294Z ```
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7194493Z legal question
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7194728Z   -> OpenCaseLaw retrieval / citation expansion
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7195028Z   -> normalized query_result_bundle
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7195324Z   -> reranking / source packing
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7195623Z   -> generative sourced answer
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7196186Z   -> independent counter-authority pass
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7196554Z   -> query-conditioned clustering / projection
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7196933Z   -> interactive map + decision/source inspection
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7197320Z ```
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7197433Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7197668Z The product does NOT require one universal geometry for all Swiss case law.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7198017Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7198909Z OpenCaseLaw is the default Swiss public data plane. The legacy 174k LexMachina corpus, global-map artifacts and research results are preserved as reusable evidence/components, not as the MVP critical path.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7199751Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7199904Z ## Central integration contract: query_result_bundle
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7200167Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7200582Z All parallel work should converge on a small product-owned bundle contract rather than inventing incompatible pipelines.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7201132Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7201258Z Minimum conceptual fields:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7201548Z - query + query variants/provenance;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7201868Z - generated answer + cited decision IDs;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7202456Z - decisions with stable decision_id, canonical URL/citation, court/date/language and retrieved text/snippets;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7203081Z - retrieval/rerank scores and source provenance;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7203478Z - counter-authority status + uncertainty/evidence;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7203829Z - cluster ID/label;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7204083Z - projection coordinates;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7204397Z - citation/typed relations.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7204578Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7205097Z Product may evolve the exact schema while preserving backwards-compatible fixtures during the MVP.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7205536Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7205641Z ## Reuse-first product shell
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7205824Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7206111Z The accepted `lab/product` implementation is a component library, not discarded legacy.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7206506Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7206611Z Prefer adapting:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7206894Z - threaded HTTP server, caching and error handling;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7207329Z - search/navigation/decision/citation/neighbor API patterns;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7207720Z - WebGL + Canvas rendering;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7207999Z - cluster/decision inspection;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7208287Z - spatial index, LOD and culling;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7208604Z - TF-IDF / clustering / UMAP / Leiden utilities;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7209148Z - multilingual/evaluation helpers.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7209348Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7209815Z Do not rebuild these unless old global-174k assumptions make adaptation slower than isolation behind the query_result_bundle seam.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7210376Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7210494Z ## Parallel engineering topology
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7210684Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7210908Z ### Core Product — continuous integrator
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7211301Z Owns the runnable application and end-to-end contract. It:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7211717Z - builds its own vertical slice continuously;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7212095Z - inspects ACCEPTED Frontier mounts every cycle;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7212459Z - absorbs useful components immediately;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7212780Z - never waits for every Frontier team;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7213121Z - keeps running until `human_gate_ready=true`.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7213358Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7213536Z ### Core Evaluation — continuous falsifier
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7214827Z Owns compact executable benchmarks for retrieval, counter-authority recall, source validity, language robustness, answer citation validity, cluster stability, reproducibility and latency. It feeds concrete failures back to Product without blocking the first clickable slice.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7215989Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7216132Z ### Human-authorized Frontier engineering teams
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7216638Z Current portfolio may run independent non-overlapping implementation tracks such as:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7217286Z - OpenCaseLaw retrieval/cache adapter;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7217678Z - generative answer + adversarial/counter-authority engine;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7218063Z - query-map UI adapter.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7218234Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7218664Z Frontier artifacts live in their own namespace and are promoted only after independent audit. Product remains the integrator.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7219358Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7219462Z ## Legacy core lanes
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7219610Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7219705Z ### Corpus
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7220350Z Historical corpus acquisition/normalization work is preserved and PAUSED. Reopen only for a concrete product capability missing from OpenCaseLaw.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7220991Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7221085Z ### Legal Distance
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7221811Z Historical representation/distance research is preserved and PAUSED. Reopen only if query-specific retrieval/map tests expose a precise representation deficit.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7222519Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7222631Z ### Fractal Map
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7223305Z Historical global hierarchy work is preserved and PAUSED. Reuse clustering/rendering code; do not repair the universal 174k map unless a query-specific product need proves it necessary.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7223785Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7223863Z ## Control plane
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7223958Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7224435Z `main` owns mission, agents, workflows, directives and factory direction. Persistent lab branches execute the latest control plane from `main`; stale role definitions on lab branches are not authoritative.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7224958Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7225356Z A cycle works on an isolated branch. Independent audit gates promotion. Rejected work never silently becomes accepted state.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7225707Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7225775Z Accepted branches:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7225948Z - `lab/corpus`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7226118Z - `lab/legal-distance`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7226292Z - `lab/fractal-map`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7226455Z - `lab/evaluation`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7226621Z - `lab/product`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7226792Z - dynamic `lab/frontier/<team_id>`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7226930Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7227009Z ## Autonomous throughput doctrine
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7227144Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7227327Z Repository-owner attention is the scarce resource; autonomous agent cycles are cheap.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7227586Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7227650Z Therefore:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7227845Z - direction changes cancel superseded same-lane work;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7228165Z - technical/network/model failures retry or rotate automatically;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7228560Z - multiple healthy free OpenCode models should be load-balanced when available;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7229097Z - independent engineering tracks run in parallel;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7229442Z - Product integrates incrementally rather than waiting for portfolio completion;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7229844Z - agents choose libraries/layouts/thresholds/repair strategies autonomously;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7230388Z - human escalation is reserved for a ready-to-test product or an unavoidable owner-level product/business/legal/external-access decision.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7230763Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7230834Z ## Output layout
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7231132Z - lane implementation: `corpus/`, `legal_distance/`, `fractal_map/`, `evaluation/`, `product/`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7231473Z - tests: `tests/<lane>/`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7231669Z - immutable outputs: `results/<lane>/`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7231887Z - reports: `reports/<lane>/`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7232094Z - accepted lane state: `state/<lane>.json`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7232335Z - lane directives: `directives/lanes/<lane>.md`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7232702Z - dynamic Frontier: `frontier/<team>/`, `results/frontier/<team>/`, `state/frontier/<team>.json`
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7232972Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7233035Z ## Invariants
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7233350Z - At most one active run per core lane or Frontier team, but different lanes/teams should run in parallel.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7233955Z - Newer direction/charter work supersedes stale same-lane/team work.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7234257Z - PASS required for accepted promotion.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7234544Z - Audit REVISE means concrete repair; BLOCKED prevents dishonest loops.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7234836Z - Supervisor dispatch is idempotent.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7235073Z - A repair cannot succeed with zero durable delta.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7235341Z - Historical accepted/negative evidence is preserved.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7235811Z - Human-authorized Frontier charters remain active until their stop/promote rule is met or an ACCEPTED equivalent supersedes them.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7236381Z - Product does not stop at a partial milestone; `human_gate_ready=true` is the normal handoff point.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7236664Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7236756Z ## Active vs historical control state
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7237764Z `state/frontier_portfolio.json` contains only executable/current Frontier teams. Retired/superseded charters are moved intact to `state/archive/frontier_portfolio_history.json`; their full implementation/audit evidence remains on lab/cycle branches. Active blockers live only under `state/blockers/`; retired blockers belong under `state/archive/blockers/`.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7238803Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7239566Z `main` is deliberately lightweight. Full result arrays, parquet files, benchmark dumps and historical reports must NOT be mirrored to main. `results/accepted-state/` plus `results/ACCEPTED_CATALOG.json` are the compact accepted-state index; detailed artifacts live on the accepted lab branch that produced them.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7240350Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7240428Z ## Progressive query execution
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7240835Z The UI should become useful in stages instead of blocking on one monolithic request:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7241172Z 1. retrieve/dedupe broad candidates;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7241384Z 2. render an initial query map;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7241646Z 3. enrich selected evidence and stream/generate the sourced answer;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7242134Z 4. run adversarial retrieval/classification;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7242592Z 5. patch counter-authorities/relations into the existing bundle/map.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7242933Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7243755Z The broad map pool and LLM evidence pack are deliberately different sizes. Query-specific mode must not load global 174k matrices on startup. Full-text decision bodies are lazy. Expensive geometry is cached by retrieval/config hash.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7244568Z === LANE ===
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7244905Z # Product lane — query-map fast path
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7245128Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7245659Z Ship the shortest runnable path to the canonical query-map MVP in `docs/product/QUERY_MAP_MVP.md`, while minimizing repository-owner attention.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7246276Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7246390Z ## REUSE-FIRST mandate
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7247216Z Before writing replacement infrastructure, inspect the existing `lab/product` implementation and accepted peer mounts. Reuse working components whenever they shorten time-to-clickable-product. In particular, prefer adapting the existing:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7248397Z - stdlib threaded HTTP server and response cache;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7248977Z - search / decision-detail / citation / neighbor API patterns;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7249391Z - WebGL + Canvas frontend;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7249696Z - clustering / Leiden / UMAP utilities;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7250125Z - map loading, navigation, LOD / culling and spatial-index patterns;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7250657Z - multilingual robustness and proximity/evaluation utilities.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7250963Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7251403Z Do NOT rebuild these just because the product mission changed. Delete/replace code only when the old global-174k assumptions make reuse slower than adaptation.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7251824Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7251904Z ## Product fast path
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7252137Z The first priority is a runnable vertical slice, not a report.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7252338Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7252604Z A valid producer cycle must materially advance executable code toward:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7253259Z question -> OpenCaseLaw retrieval/cache -> query result bundle -> free reranking -> sourced generative answer -> independent counter-authority pass -> query-specific clickable map.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7253739Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7253894Z For the first clickable slice, simple and correct beats sophisticated:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7254303Z - target roughly 100–300 retrieved decisions;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7254566Z - TF-IDF/BM25 + citation expansion is acceptable;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7254916Z - simple deterministic clustering/projection is acceptable;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7255404Z - reuse the current frontend rather than redesigning it;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7255826Z - 2D is acceptable; 3D is explicitly NOT a blocker;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7256413Z - a cached OpenCaseLaw fixture is acceptable for deterministic tests while live retrieval remains available.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7256720Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7256844Z ## Anti-overengineering
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7257040Z Do NOT spend an MVP cycle on:
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7257239Z - universal 174k alignment;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7257454Z - rebuilding the Swiss corpus/citation graph;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7257689Z - dense 174k embedding generation;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7257894Z - global fractal hierarchy;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7258090Z - custom model training;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7258351Z - requiring the owner to provision paid inference for development/testing;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7258641Z - cosmetic redesign;
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7259122Z - broad architecture prose before a vertical slice exists.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7259386Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7259665Z ## Cycle output requirement
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7260172Z Every normal product cycle must leave runnable code or tests. A cycle that produces only plans/reports/specs is REVISE unless execution is genuinely externally blocked.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7260618Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7261415Z The first successful product cycle should, at minimum, allow a developer to run one local command/server, submit or select a real Swiss-law query fixture, and see a source-linked clickable result map. Generative answer/counter-authority functionality should be added in the same cycle if feasible; otherwise it is the immediate next delta.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7262265Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7262846Z Do not involve the owner during ordinary implementation/debugging. Continue autonomously through retries, narrower slices and repairs until there is a genuinely clickable end-to-end artifact worth testing, or an unavoidable owner-level decision.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7263476Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7263555Z ## Owner-attention rule
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7264388Z Agent cycles are cheap; owner attention is expensive. There is no fixed cycle limit while executable progress continues. If a cycle stalls, diagnose and reroute autonomously. Do not ask the owner to choose technical details or babysit failures. The next normal owner interaction should be a usable product test.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7265667Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7265767Z ## Parallel integration rule
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7267059Z Three human-authorized Frontier engineering teams may produce retrieval, generative-audit, and query-map UI components in parallel. Do NOT wait for all teams. At the start of every product cycle, inspect ACCEPTED mounts under /tmp/lex_accepted/frontier and immediately absorb any component that passes its integration contract.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7268566Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7269346Z Product remains responsible for the end-to-end app and may implement the same missing seam itself if a Frontier team is slow. Frontier teams are accelerators, not dependencies.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7270111Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7271111Z Until the product state explicitly records `human_gate_ready: true` with a locally runnable question -> sourced answer -> counter-authority -> clickable map path, keep `continue_recommended: true`. A partial milestone is not a reason for the lane to stop.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7272345Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7272456Z ## Runtime performance mandate
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7274161Z The query-map hot path must be lightweight. Do not initialize legacy 174k representations on default server startup. Render the first query-specific candidate map before waiting for the LLM/counter-authority pass. Fetch full decisions lazily for the evidence subset/clicked cases, not all mapped cases. Use persistent cache + bounded concurrency + deterministic cache/config hashes.
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7275753Z 
2026-11-13T05:37:58.7278214Z Target: cached map <1s; after the first upstream search page arrives, local map overhead <1.5s; render the first ~50–100 results immediately and expand toward 100–300 in background; local 100–300 point geometry <2s; detail click <150ms where data is local. Measure upstream OpenCaseLaw latency separately rather than blaming local code. Treat these as engineering budgets and measure them. Prefer simpler clustering/projection when sophistication misses the budget without demonstrated UX benefit.
