2026-11-13T05:38:02.4564742Z # LexMachina — Query Map MVP
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4564984Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4565107Z Status: CANONICAL PRODUCT TARGET
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4565411Z Date: 2026-10-11
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4565572Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4565688Z ## 1. Product purpose
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4565855Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4566255Z LexMachina is a legal research interface, not a project to discover one universal geometry of all Swiss case law.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4566779Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4567758Z The user asks a legal research question. LexMachina must return:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4568155Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4568277Z 1. a sourced AI answer;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4568628Z 2. the relevant cases used to support that answer;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4569169Z 3. a visual map of the broader retrieved jurisprudence;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4569943Z 4. an explicit adversarial search for cases that contradict, limit, distinguish, or create exceptions to the provisional answer.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4570534Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4571267Z The visual map exists to help a jurist see structure that a ranked text list can hide: minority lines, isolated cases, alternative doctrinal branches, and unexpected bridges between groups.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4572081Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4572205Z ## 2. Core product loop
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4572377Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4572472Z For a query Q:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4572625Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4572783Z 1. Retrieve broadly from OpenCaseLaw.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4573249Z 2. Expand around strong candidates using citations where useful.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4573750Z 3. Preserve a high-recall candidate pool.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4574393Z 4. Rank / filter to a tractable map set (target: 100–300 decisions for the first MVP).
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4575026Z 5. Independently search for contrary / limiting / distinguishing authorities.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4575607Z 6. Build a query-specific similarity / relation graph.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4576104Z 7. Cluster and project that graph into an interactive map.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4602712Z 8. Generate concise cluster labels with provenance.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4603135Z 9. Produce a sourced AI answer.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4603550Z 10. Let the user inspect any decision, cluster, relation, or contrary authority.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4603927Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4604238Z The same decision may occupy a different position for a different query. This is expected.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4604703Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4604817Z ## 3. Data source
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4604962Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4605240Z Primary Swiss public source: OpenCaseLaw public REST/MCP infrastructure.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4605595Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4605700Z Requirements:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4605949Z - no paid API key;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4606290Z - no login dependency for core public endpoints;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4607019Z - cache retrieved records locally for reproducibility;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4607434Z - preserve source URLs / decision IDs;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4607858Z - fail gracefully if the remote service is unavailable;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4608546Z - do not rebuild OpenCaseLaw's national corpus or citation graph unless a product-critical capability is missing.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4609321Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4609901Z The legacy 174k corpus and its artifacts remain preserved as research evidence and optional fallback/test data, but are no longer the critical path.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4610564Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4610712Z ## 4. Owner-time invariant
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4610874Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4611179Z The scarce resource is **the repository owner's attention**, not agent compute.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4611547Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4612055Z For development and testing, the canonical path must work without requiring the owner to buy or provision paid inference. Prefer:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4612779Z - OpenCaseLaw public API / MCP;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4613229Z - OpenCode free models / healthy free fallbacks;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4613671Z - locally runnable open-source models;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4613995Z - open-source Python/JS libraries;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4614318Z - existing repository artifacts.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4614519Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4615403Z This is a development/test constraint, NOT a permanent product architecture constraint. A future production service may use paid or hosted LLM/embedding/reranking infrastructure if that improves the product and has a viable business case.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4616459Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4617207Z The factory must not trade away product quality or create needless engineering solely to avoid hypothetical future inference cost.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4617829Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4617937Z Owner-attention rules:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4618211Z - technical failures auto-retry or reroute;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4618801Z - implementation choices inside the canonical mission are made autonomously;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4619442Z - do not ask the owner to choose libraries, embeddings, layouts, thresholds, or repair strategies;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4620084Z - do not ask for manual data preparation that agents can perform;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4621062Z - surface a human gate only when a clickable product is ready for judgment, or when an unavoidable product/business/legal/external-access choice genuinely requires the owner.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4621861Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4621973Z ## 5. Retrieval-first doctrine
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4622181Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4622376Z A visualizer cannot reveal a case that retrieval never found.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4622699Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4622957Z Therefore the first product metric is retrieval coverage, not map beauty.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4623338Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4623516Z The pipeline should combine free techniques as useful:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4623932Z - OpenCaseLaw lexical / filtered search;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4624282Z - query expansion in DE/FR/IT;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4624600Z - exact norm / citation retrieval;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4624934Z - citation-neighborhood expansion;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4625254Z - TF-IDF / BM25 reranking;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4625648Z - existing accepted LexMachina representations where they help;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4626403Z - optional open-source multilingual embeddings if they improve retrieval on frozen tests without paid inference.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4626958Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4627212Z Do not build a new universal 174k embedding space merely to satisfy this MVP.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4627587Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4627732Z ## 6. Adversarial / counter-authority pass
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4627972Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4628452Z After drafting a provisional answer, run an independent retrieval pass whose instruction is to find authorities that could:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4629176Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4629319Z - contradict the provisional conclusion;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4629650Z - narrow it;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4629920Z - distinguish the factual/legal situation;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4630473Z - reveal an exception;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4630752Z - show a minority or older line;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4631083Z - expose a language-specific branch;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4631438Z - undermine the apparent consensus.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4631653Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4631955Z These cases must be retained in the map even when their initial relevance score is lower.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4632376Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4633142Z The UI must distinguish "supporting", "limiting", "contrary/exception", and "unclassified" only when the classification is actually supported. Uncertain classifications must remain uncertain.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4634016Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4634130Z ## 7. Query-specific map
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4634310Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4634733Z The map is generated from the retrieved set, not from a claim that all Swiss cases possess one canonical global position.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4635284Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4635388Z Minimum map semantics:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4635673Z - point = decision;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4636066Z - spatial proximity = query-conditioned similarity / relation strength;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4636565Z - cluster = locally coherent result group;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4636973Z - visible outliers = isolated or weakly connected decisions;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4637429Z - citation/relation edges available on selection;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4637855Z - counter-authorities visually discoverable;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4638260Z - cluster labels explain why the group exists.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4638531Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4639439Z 2D or 3D is an implementation choice. 3D is useful only if it increases comprehension. A beautiful 3D point cloud with no readable legal structure fails.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4640146Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4640256Z ## 8. AI answer
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4640405Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4640557Z The AI answer and the map are complementary.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4640813Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4640933Z Answer requirements:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4641229Z - answer the legal question;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4641597Z - cite decisions actually retrieved from the source;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4642042Z - separate strong propositions from uncertainty;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4642629Z - mention material counter-authorities / exceptions surfaced by the adversarial pass;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4643346Z - provide links / identifiers so the user can inspect the underlying decision.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4643756Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4644113Z The map must remain available after the answer so the user can independently audit what the AI said.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4644609Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4644714Z ## 9. MVP UI
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4644859Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4644985Z One page is enough.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4645145Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4645253Z Required:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4645506Z - search / question input;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4645813Z - sourced answer panel;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4646097Z - interactive map;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4646358Z - result count;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4646611Z - cluster labels;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4646876Z - decision detail panel;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4647203Z - toggle / emphasis for counter-authorities;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4647592Z - relation edges on selection;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4647927Z - search within current result set;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4648257Z - reset / fit view.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4648411Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4648548Z Nice-to-have, not MVP blockers:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4649039Z - 3D terrain;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4649283Z - animation;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4649538Z - full corpus browse mode;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4649835Z - custom corpus import;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4650115Z - multiple legal views.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4650296Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4650422Z ## 9A. Performance architecture
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4650631Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4651331Z Performance is part of the product hypothesis. A visually auditable system that feels materially slower than ordinary legal search will fail even if its clusters are good.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4652308Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4652433Z ### Progressive pipeline
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4652614Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4652793Z Do NOT serialize the whole query path behind the LLM.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4653087Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4653191Z Preferred flow:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4653491Z 1. normalize query + check persistent cache;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4654005Z 2. run broad OpenCaseLaw search/query variants with bounded concurrency;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4654570Z 3. deduplicate and return the first ranked candidate set;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4655079Z 4. compute a fast initial query-specific map and render it;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4655759Z 5. in parallel, fetch richer text/structure only for the evidence subset needed for answer generation;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4656430Z 6. stream/generate the sourced answer;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4657049Z 7. run the adversarial/counter-authority pass in parallel or immediately after the provisional answer;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4657834Z 8. incrementally update the map/statuses when additional authorities are found.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4658249Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4658557Z The initial map MUST NOT wait for completion of the generative answer or adversarial pass.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4659130Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4659244Z ### Hot-path constraints
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4659433Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4659842Z - Query-specific mode must not initialize/load the legacy 174k global-map representations at server startup.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4660541Z - Legacy artifacts are lazy/optional fallback only.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4662195Z - Do not fetch full text for all 100–300 mapped cases before first render. Use search/regeste/snippet metadata for broad-map geometry; lazily fetch full decision/structure for the smaller answer-evidence set and clicked cases.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4663460Z - Deduplicate before expensive full-text/network/LLM work.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4664081Z - Use bounded concurrent remote calls while respecting OpenCaseLaw pacing/rate limits.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4664939Z - Persist query/result/source caches to disk so repeated queries and test fixtures avoid repeated network work.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4665977Z - Separate the broad map pool from the answer context. The LLM should receive a selected evidence pack, not 300 complete judgments.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4666812Z - Cache expensive map geometry by query + retrieval/config hash.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4667446Z - Do not recompute unchanged clusters/projection merely because answer text changed.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4667874Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4667990Z ### MVP latency budgets
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4668159Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4668340Z These are engineering targets, not scientific claims:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4669088Z - lightweight server startup: target < 3 s excluding first-time local model download/start;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4669693Z - cached query to initial map: target < 1 s;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4670617Z - upstream search latency is external (OpenCaseLaw currently documents roughly 5–15 s typical search latency); measure it separately;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4671711Z - after the first OpenCaseLaw result page arrives, local normalize/rerank/geometry/render overhead: target < 1.5 s;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4672851Z - first map may render from the first ~50–100 results; expand incrementally toward ~100–300 without clearing/freezing the UI;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4673770Z - local clustering/projection for ~100–300 decisions: target < 2 s;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4674378Z - decision click/detail from already fetched data: target < 150 ms locally;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4675040Z - answer generation should stream or expose progress rather than block the map;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4675729Z - counter-authority updates may arrive later, but must not freeze the interface.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4676146Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4677062Z Record measured p50/p95-like timings for frozen fixtures/live smoke tests where practical. If UMAP/Leiden or another sophisticated method violates the budget without measurable UX gain, fall back to the simpler method.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4678088Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4678396Z ### Memory/startup discipline
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4678570Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4679349Z The query-map MVP should run without loading corpus-scale matrices into RAM. Existing 174k assets are reusable research components but are not allowed on the default hot path.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4680137Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4680270Z ## 10. Reuse from existing LexMachina
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4680493Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4680619Z Reuse only when it reduces time-to-test:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4680971Z - existing TF-IDF / lexical tooling;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4681302Z - multilingual robustness tests;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4681626Z - clustering / hierarchy code;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4681940Z - WebGL / Canvas rendering;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4682230Z - LOD / culling;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4682508Z - decision detail / navigation components;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4682884Z - benchmark discipline and negative results.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4683122Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4683237Z Do NOT block the MVP on:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4683755Z - global 174k id→cluster alignment;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4684109Z - global citation-graph reconstruction;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4684445Z - dense 174k embeddings;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4684740Z - universal fractal hierarchy;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4685197Z - BGE/bger crosswalk work beyond what the new query pipeline actually needs.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4685582Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4685700Z ## 10A. Reuse-first inventory
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4685889Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4686367Z The product pivot does **not** invalidate the month of prior LexMachina work. Reuse existing implementation before replacing it.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4686937Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4687094Z Known reusable assets on `lab/product` include:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4688025Z - `product/server.py`: threaded stdlib HTTP server, response cache, rate limiting, health/error patterns and API routing;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4689244Z - `product/static/index.html`: existing interactive WebGL/Canvas map UI, search/filter controls and decision/cluster interaction patterns;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4690177Z - `product/app/navigation.py`: navigation/search/decision/neighbor/citation API patterns;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4690813Z - `product/app/map_loader.py`: representation/map loading contracts;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4691534Z - existing clustering/projection tooling based on scikit-learn, NetworkX, igraph/Leiden and UMAP;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4692276Z - existing spatial-index, LOD/culling, proximity-explanation and import patterns;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4693155Z - accepted evaluation work on multilingual robustness, jurist preference, boilerplate resistance and deterministic benchmarking.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4693723Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4693831Z Reuse rule:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4694108Z 1. adapt before rewriting;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4694451Z 2. preserve historical artifacts and negative results;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4695271Z 3. if an old global-174k assumption blocks adaptation, isolate it behind a new query-bundle adapter rather than replacing the whole server/UI;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4696244Z 4. the preferred new abstraction is a `query_result_bundle` consumed by the existing product shell.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4696712Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4696863Z Suggested minimum `query_result_bundle` fields:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4697217Z - query;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4697469Z - generated_answer + cited decision IDs;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4697853Z - retrieval metadata/provenance;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4701155Z - decisions[];
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4701439Z - per-decision retrieval/rerank scores;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4701778Z - counter_authority_status with uncertainty;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4702016Z - cluster_id / cluster_label;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4702223Z - x/y (and optional z) projection;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4702451Z - typed relations/citations;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4702662Z - source URL / citation string.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4702786Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4702890Z ## 10B. Autonomous execution / anti-drift rule
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4703050Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4703347Z The MVP should not need another open-ended research program, but **there is no arbitrary limit on free autonomous agent cycles**.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4703872Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4703954Z Preferred milestone sequence:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4704392Z - first usable vertical slice: real OpenCaseLaw/cached query -> query_result_bundle -> source-linked clickable map using reused UI/server;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4704988Z - next: sourced generative answer + independent counter-authority pass integrated into that same UI;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4705505Z - then: autonomous fixes driven by evaluation until the product is ready for the human product gate.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4705795Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4706551Z Agents may iterate as long as they are making measurable progress. Repeated cycles with no executable delta must trigger autonomous diagnosis, rerouting or narrower implementation — not a request for owner intervention.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4707129Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4707232Z The relevant cost metric is owner attention:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4707542Z - zero owner involvement during routine implementation/debugging;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4707911Z - one owner checkpoint when a genuinely usable end-to-end product is ready;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4708370Z - additional owner involvement only for a true product decision that autonomous evidence cannot resolve.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4708669Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4709050Z ## 11. Automated evaluation
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4709252Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4709859Z Create a small frozen set of real Swiss legal research questions with known useful authorities and at least some known limiting / contrary authority where feasible.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4710552Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4710652Z Measure:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4711068Z - recall of known relevant authorities;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4711430Z - recall of known counter-authorities;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4711725Z - duplication rate;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4711968Z - language robustness;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4712221Z - source validity;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4712446Z - cluster stability;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4712681Z - latency;
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4712926Z - deterministic reproducibility of cached runs.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4713164Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4713340Z Do not pretend these automated tests prove UX usefulness.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4713611Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4713728Z ## 12. Human product gate
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4713896Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4714341Z The MVP earns further investment only if a jurist can use it on real research questions and answer YES to at least two of the following:
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4714900Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4715260Z 1. The map exposed a relevant branch / case / exception that was less visible in the ranked list or AI answer.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4715937Z 2. The map made the structure of the jurisprudence easier to understand.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4716551Z 3. The map increased confidence that contrary authority had not simply been hidden by the answer.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4717196Z 4. The combined answer + map was preferable to a conventional answer + result list.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4717564Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4717927Z If this does not happen on a small set of real research tasks, STOP investing in LexMachina as a standalone product.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4718373Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4718499Z ## 13. Immediate implementation order
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4722643Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4722952Z ### Milestone A — end-to-end free query pipeline
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4723629Z OpenCaseLaw query → cached candidate set → free reranking → AI answer → JSON result bundle.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4724028Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4724198Z ### Milestone B — adversarial retrieval
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4724868Z Independent counter-authority search → merge/deduplicate → classify conservatively → expose in result bundle.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4725343Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4725505Z ### Milestone C — clickable query map
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4726075Z 100–300 decisions → similarity/relation graph → clusters → projection → interactive browser UI.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4726469Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4726622Z ### Milestone D — product evaluation
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4727695Z Frozen benchmark queries + human test. Only after this gate should the factory spend effort on more sophisticated geometry, 3D, dense embeddings, or large-scale custom infrastructure.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4728405Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4728496Z ## 14. Kill rule
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4728632Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4729711Z If repeated autonomous work cannot produce a clickable end-to-end prototype without consuming repeated owner attention, record that as a failure of the autonomous-development approach and simplify/reroute before asking the owner to intervene.
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4730706Z 
2026-11-13T05:38:02.4731430Z The substantive kill rule is product usefulness: if a working prototype shows that the visual layer does not materially improve legal research over answer + ranked list, stop the standalone product.
