2026-11-13T05:39:16.4225055Z #!/usr/bin/env python3
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4225439Z """Audit-ready diagnosis of an operational-resume snapshot.
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4225778Z 
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4226040Z An operational resume starts from a *persisted producer snapshot* after a
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4226704Z failed workflow.  Two independent questions must be answered before the
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4227184Z snapshot can be handed to an auditor:
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4227408Z 
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4227657Z 1. **Why did the run stop before a gate?** - answered from the committed
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4228282Z    public run/jobs snapshot by :mod:`product.audit_step_diagnosis` (no token,
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4229069Z    no job logs, no invented mechanism).
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4229559Z 2. **Does the persisted snapshot carry a durable delta at all?** - answered
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4230442Z    from git refs alone.  A snapshot equal to its predecessor's commit is
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4231042Z    ``ZERO_DURABLE_DELTA``: the workflow's ``if: always()`` persist step
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4231634Z    published the unchanged tree after the failed producer step, so the ref
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4232076Z    exists but proves no work.
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4232253Z 
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4232480Z The module also records, read-only, whether this run has either half of
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4233084Z factory-wide requirement 4 (an independent audit gate and an accept commit),
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4233713Z and whether the producer wrote anything into the auditor namespace.  It never
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4234342Z writes ``results/audit/**``, never mints a gate, and never labels a run
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4234803Z accepted or rejected.
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4234982Z 
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4235078Z Usage
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4235302Z -----
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4235593Z     python3 product/resume_snapshot_diagnosis.py \\
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4236077Z         --run-id 40193974025 --predecessor-run-id 40188639817 \\
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4236662Z         --raw results/product/orchestration/CYCLE_40193974025_team_step_raw.json \\
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4237327Z         --out results/product/orchestration/CYCLE_40193974025_resume_diagnosis.json
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4237708Z 
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4237981Z When no public run/jobs snapshot was captured for the resumed run (for example
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4238654Z an operational resume dispatched straight from a failed run whose logs are not
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4239614Z reachable from the producer environment), omit ``--raw``: the instrument then
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4240510Z records ``RAW_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE`` / ``mechanism_unobserved`` instead of
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4241187Z inventing a cause, while still proving the durable-delta fact from git refs.
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4241855Z ``--predecessor-ref`` (default ``origin/lab/product``) compares the snapshot
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4242492Z against the accepted head the failed run was dispatched from, which is the
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4243138Z right delta baseline for a resume run: comparing against the previous *team*
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4243846Z ref would count the accepted audit commit as if the failed run had produced it.
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4244246Z 
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4244484Z Refs must already be available locally (the workflow fetches ``main``,
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4245053Z ``lab/<lane>`` and the team ref).  The instrument never fetches, so an
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4245620Z offline reproduction is honest about a missing ref instead of silently
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4246102Z reaching the network.
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4246374Z """
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4246650Z from __future__ import annotations
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4246864Z 
2026-11-13T05:39:16.4246977Z import argparse
