2026-11-13T05:40:35.0694877Z #!/usr/bin/env python3
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0695270Z """Frozen D2/D3/D4 content-defect re-probe over the committed bundle family.
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0695618Z 
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0695725Z Why this exists
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0695952Z ---------------
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0696305Z Direction v68 ordered work item (2) asks the product to *publish* a per-bundle
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0696716Z and per-class histogram of the frozen D2/D3/D4 content predicates over the
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0697116Z flagship offline/server slice family, together with the false-reject count on
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0697488Z the confirmed set, instead of restating the result as prose in
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0697849Z ``state/product.json``.  Until this module existed the only statement of that
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0698199Z result was the narrative line
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0698389Z 
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0698616Z     "All 4 offline slice bundles and the server slice bundle regenerated with
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0699441Z      the fix show correct downgrades"
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0699656Z 
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0699881Z which no committed instrument re-derived.  This module is that instrument.
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0700240Z 
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0700405Z What it measures (and what it deliberately does not)
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0700814Z ----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0701321Z For every committed ``*.bundle.json`` under ``results/product/offline_slice/``
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0701760Z and ``results/product/server_slice/`` it applies the product's own frozen
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0702166Z content predicates (``product.query.counter_evidence_span.frozen_content_defects``)
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0702774Z to every row that is still ``counter_evidence_verified is True`` and counts the
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0703140Z defect classes that survive on the *shipped* (post-filter) bytes.
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0703350Z 
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0703557Z * ``fixed_path_family`` — bundles whose provenance carries
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0703910Z   ``provenance.counter_evidence_span.content_filter``, i.e. bundles that were
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0704315Z   regenerated on the fixed path.  This family is *identified from the bytes*,
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0704693Z   never hard-coded, so a future regeneration is picked up automatically.
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0705135Z * ``all_committed`` — every committed bundle, including historical ones that
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0705852Z   predate the fix.  Historical defects are preserved evidence, not a defect of
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0706493Z   the current head; both populations are published side by side so the two are
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0706942Z   never conflated.
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0707526Z * ``before_after`` — for the four decisions the accepted FAST-MVP falsifier
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0708100Z   measured as verified-but-defective, the seam's own per-row downgrade records
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0708655Z   on the fixed path are paired with the historical verified verdict: same
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0709373Z   decision, BEFORE verified+defective, AFTER unevidenced with a reason code.
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0711452Z   The confirmed sound row is re-checked in the same pass.  No historical
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0712231Z   bundle is rewritten or deleted.
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0712801Z * ``packet_v3_reemission`` — the frozen packet-of-record v3 bytes are hashed,
2026-11-13T05:40:35.0713283Z [0m
